            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0306" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/292: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-06T14:00:00-05:00">April 6, 1936—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Despatch No. 4301 from Berne concerning Inter-Governmental Conference on
                    status of refugees.</p>
                <p>This Government does not contemplate participating actively in that Conference
                    but desires that you, or in your absence a member of your staff, attend as an
                    observer. If you have any comment or suggestion to make regarding this
                    assignment please telegraph at once.</p>
                <p>Background material for your information will be transmitted by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
